# Starforge Universe site concept

Preserve this product and design concept in all UI, copy, and frontend changes.

## Brand and storytelling

- Brand name: **Starforge Universe** (hero-level, not only nav text).
- Tone: Apple-style scroll storytelling — sparse sections, one job per section, large expressive type.
- Hybrid visual system: cinematic **deep-space hero** + quieter **light paper stage** content sections.
- Support **dark and light** themes (`data-theme` on `html`, `ThemeService`, persisted). Both modes must remain viable.
- Fonts: Syne (display) + Manrope (body). Do not switch to Inter/Roboto/Arial/system stacks.
- Accents: cool starlight / teal-metal — not purple glow defaults. On light stages, use dark stage eyebrow tokens (`--sf-stage-eyebrow`) for contrast.
- Motion: ambient stars/parallax, scroll reveals, route view transitions. Prefer `opacity`/`transform`; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Navigation (no page-load feel)

- Keep app shell (ambient background + sticky nav) mounted across routes.
- Home: `''`. Product detail: `/lines/:slug`. Unknown slug: in-page missing state; unknown path: 404.
- Use `routerLink` / `Router` + `withViewTransitions()` — never full document reloads for product selection.
- Detail views always offer a clear **Back to universe** path.
- Sticky nav uses an Apple-style full-width hover mega pane. Menu entries come from catalog nested `products`, or **Coming soon** when a line has none yet. Do not hard-code mega-menu product rows in the template.
- Nav also includes **Contact**, which opens a mega pane with a friendly invite to email `star.forge.worker@starforge-universe.com` (mailto link). Contact is not a product line.

## Product lines (extendable)

- Single source of truth: [`src/app/data/product-lines.ts`](src/app/data/product-lines.ts).
- To add a product line, **only add a catalog entry** (slug, name, tagline, summary, status, story blocks). Home list and nav must stay data-driven — do not hard-code product rows in templates.
- Category lines (for example Utilities) may include nested `products`. Add tools there to extend the category without new hard-coded UI.
- Hierarchical catalogs use nested `children` (for example DevOps Template → stack templates → language archetypes). Mega menu and detail pages must render hierarchy from data. Deeper nested templates appear in a right-hand mega flyout on hover of their parent. Composition products use `composedOf` (slugs of peer templates) and show a **Composed from** flyout / detail section instead of duplicating those templates as children.
- Status may be `available`, `building`, or `retired` (retired archetypes stay listed but must not be oversold).
- Current lines:
  - `project-templating` — Starforge project templating (available): `devops-template` at the top with children `spring-template` (→ spring-library/service/application + retired spring-function), `terraform-template`, `angular-webapp-template`, `python-function-template`, `app-tap-template` (composed from terraform + angular-webapp + python-function), `database-template`, `library-template` (→ python-library-template). Composition products use `composedOf` slugs (not duplicated `children`).
  - `all-seeing-eye` — All Seeing Eye (building): discoverability and monitoring of codebase state across a project universe; dependencies/integrations for compliance; architectural overview of GitHub repos. Frame as in progress / growing — do not oversell.
  - `utilities` — Utilities (available): category of developer productivity tools. Nested `products` grow this line; first tool is LiquiSketch (Liquibase changelogs → Draw.io schema diagrams). Add more utilities via `products`, not hard-coded templates.

## Home section order

1. Hero — brand, one headline, one lead, one CTA group; no product grid in the first viewport.
2. Introduction — what Starforge Universe is.
3. Product lines — catalog-driven list linking to details.
4. Closing — quiet invitation; universe still expanding.

## Hero visual (orbit + canvas sphere)

The hero right column is a **deep-space focal object**: CSS orbit rings plus a **canvas-rendered 3D sphere** in `.hero__core` (not a CSS gradient disc or static image).

- **Layout:** `.hero__visual` holds two animated `.hero__orbit` ellipses and `.hero__core` with `.hero__sphere-canvas`. Keep copy in `.hero__content`; do not overlay cards, badges, or promo chips on the sphere.
- **Renderer:** [`src/app/components/home/hero-sphere.canvas.ts`](src/app/components/home/hero-sphere.canvas.ts) owns draw logic; [`src/app/components/home/home.component.ts`](src/app/components/home/home.component.ts) owns the rAF loop, `ResizeObserver`, and canvas sizing.
- **Cycle (20s, repeating):** **15s solid** globe → **5s wireframe** mesh. Both phases share the same Y-axis spin rate so rotation never jumps at transitions.
- **Phase transitions:** brief **TV signal-loss glitch** (solid / wireframe / blank flicker + scan lines) centered on each phase change. Keep glitch short and cinematic — not a loading spinner.
- **Solid phase:** smooth per-pixel sphere with **view-fixed front/camera lighting** (curvature + soft center specular). It must read as a lit 3D globe without a rotating dark hemisphere or side-biased highlight. Do not reintroduce back-face culling holes or strong directional lights tied to rotated normals.
- **Wireframe phase:** **lines only** — no solid body fill under the mesh. Lat/lon grid uses the same 3D projection/tilt as the solid shape.
- **Palette:** cool starlight / teal-metal (`rgba(168, 212, 224, …)` strokes, teal solid fill, soft outer glow). No purple glow defaults.
- **Glow:** radial halo must stay **inside the canvas bounds** (no square clip artifact). `.hero__core` uses `border-radius: 50%` and `overflow: hidden`.
- **Retina / DPR:** pass **logical** canvas size into `drawHeroSphere`; vector draws use the context transform, `putImageData` uses device pixels explicitly.
- **Motion accessibility:** when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, render one static solid frame — no cycle, glitch, or spin.

## Do not

- Replace the hybrid cosmic/stage system with a generic dashboard or purple-gradient AI look.
- Put cards, badges, or promo chips on top of hero media.
- Replace the hero canvas sphere with a flat CSS circle, faceted mesh solid, or image that loses the solid/wireframe cycle.
- Duplicate product copy outside the catalog when the catalog already owns it.
